        "date": "2026-11-24T17:36:50Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(tools): add metric tap-drill and clearance drills, a 3 mm ball and a 6 mm bull nose to the catalog\n\nThe starter catalog gets 16 tools: BN-0300, BB-0600-R1, and a tap drill\nand a clearance drill (ISO 273 medium) for each coarse thread M3-M12.\nEach tool goes into its family in diameter order. The cutting data\nfollows the catalog's own rows (docs/decisions/3036-metric-catalog.md).\nDrill flute lengths are on a 0.5 mm step, so the spun holder stacks\nbit-identically to the cylinder.\n\nFixes #3036\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
